WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:05.000
When it comes to Marvel trailers, every moment
has something important to say and comes with

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.160
the promise of deeper meanings, hidden explanations,
and misleading misdirections.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:13.100
Let's break it down and take a look at more
details you may have missed in the newest

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.100
Avengers: Endgame trailer.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.400
The new trailer featured a group of heroes
walking through the Avengers hangar.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.360
If the scene from the trailer felt familiar,
there's a good reason for that: The Super

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.939
Bowl spot also ended on a quick tease of a
string of heroes walking through the same

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:26.440
hangar.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:30.460
The thing is, each trailer seems to be showing
distinctly different groups of people at different

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:30.960
times.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:36.039
The Big Game clip seemed to depict Cap, Thor,
Black Widow, Rocket, Ant-Man, War Machine,

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.899
and either Bruce Banner or Clint Barton.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.680
They also appear to be wearing their normal
super-suits.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:45.760
This time around the setting remained, but
the shot showed Cap, Ant-Man, Hawkeye, War

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.780
Machine, Black Widow, Iron Man AND Nebula
- all sporting new suits that look an awful

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:55.479
lot like a variation on Hank Pym's Quantum
Realm suit, or even the space armor that the

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.100
heroes donned in the cartoons.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:58.380
What's going on here?

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:02.459
Why do we have two nearly identical shots
with completely different groups and suits?

00:01:02.459 --> 00:01:04.350
"What do you think is happening right now?"

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:05.390
"It doesn't matter."

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:05.880
"It's good."

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:10.799
Whenever Endgame takes place, speculation
is running high that it will showcase a sizable

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.040
jump forward in time.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:16.350
In the newest trailer we get a clip of Clint
Barton with what appears to be his family.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:20.490
The next shot is a repeat from the last trailer,
showing a distressed Barton with a completely

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:21.619
different haircut.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:22.700
Then there's Black Widow.

00:01:22.829 --> 00:01:26.940
She ended Infinity War with short blonde hair,
but in the trailer she's shown with long hair

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:28.439
that drapes past her shoulders.

00:01:28.439 --> 00:01:33.060
Her hair also goes from blonde to her natural
red, and that takes time to grow out.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:36.619
Black Widow seems to be the big clue that
we are dealing with some sort of time jump

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:37.640
between movies.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:42.840
The first trailer had a moment showing Steve
Rogers looking at a compass with Agent Peggy

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:46.590
Carter's picture in it, a touching reminder
of how far the man has come since he was a

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:49.520
scrawny kid desperately trying to fight for
his country.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:54.030
Although apparently, it wasn't just a callback
to an emotional past, because Cap's old flame

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.800
can be heard in a voiceover during the new
trailer too.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.440
The world has changed.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.900
None of us can go back."

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:04.140
Sound familiar?

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:07.860
It's the same line she said as Cap sat by
her deathbed in Winter Soldier.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:09.580
"The world has changed.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:11.260
None of us can go back.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:12.660
All we can do is our best

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:17.660
And sometimes the best we can do is to start
over."

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:22.060
Whatever the implications might be, the appearance
of Peggy in the new trailer is starting to

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:24.540
make us wonder how she might fit into the
bigger picture.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:29.599
The slo-mo walk through the HQ hangar was
dripping with teasers, but the new suits and

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:33.710
appearance of Tony Stark and Nebula made it
easy to miss one of the biggest questions

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:37.200
that the scene posed: where were Bruce Banner,
Thor, and Carol Danvers?

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:41.220
We now know thanks to that last tag at the
end of the new trailer along with the mid-credits

00:02:41.239 --> 00:02:45.681
scene from her own movie that Danvers will
be joining up with the team, which makes her

00:02:45.681 --> 00:02:48.240
absence from the hangar scene that much more
conspicuous.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:50.500
Does the scene take place before she arrives?

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.380
The absence of both Banner and Thor is even
more puzzling.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:57.340
Both should be around from the beginning of
the film, as they were among the survivors

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:57.920
of the snap.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:01.820
We're still waiting for the three-movie arc
for Hulk that Mark Ruffalo's spoken about,

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.620
so Hulk's almost guaranteed to be in the movie
somewhere.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.360
What about Thor?

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.400
Asgard is destroyed and he has Stormbreaker,
so there's little need to be off elsewhere

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.400
on his own personal errands at this point.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.519
Why are the three most powerful members of
the team not present?

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.860
It seems like a bit of a handicap if the group
is going up against Thanos.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:22.500
Another intriguing detail is easy to miss
during that hangar walk, and it has to do

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.680
with an Avenger that typically doesn't get
much screen time: Rhodey.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:30.330
Always playing the number two to Tony, Rhodey
was nevertheless a solid presence throughout

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:34.290
Infinity War, doing everything he could to
help keep the enemy contained on the battlefield

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:34.940
of Wakanda.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.830
In fact, it seemed a shame that it was the
sheepish Banner that ended up donning that

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:42.640
Hulkbuster armor when the much more experienced
Iron Patriot was standing by.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:46.820
Fans have been looking for a War Machine decked
out in Hulkbuster armor ever since spotting

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:49.640
a Hulkbuster War Machine Lego set planned
for Endgame.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:54.000
While it doesn't come across as quite Hulkbuster
size, the armor Rhodey is wearing in the clip

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.560
is undeniably a bit beefier than normal.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:00.280
Whether the team is heading into the Quantum
Realm or space, it makes sense that Rhodey

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.920
would want a little bit more protection.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.280
Or maybe he just wanted more room to pack
weapons in.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:05.800
"I think I'll take it."

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:06.480
"Which one?"

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:08.140
"All of it."

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:12.320
The theme of the first trailer tended to revolve
around loss.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:13.360
Not so with the second.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:17.540
This time the whole message can be boiled
down to three words: "Whatever it takes."

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:18.420
"Whatever it takes."

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:23.060
"Whatever it takes."

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:26.440
"Whatever it takes."

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.440
As the group is shown in various capacities
preparing to do "whatever it takes," though,

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.620
there are four people that stand out from
the crowd.

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:38.660
First to say the line is Cap, followed by
Clint, then Natasha, then, finally, Tony Stark.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:39.940
"Whatever it takes."

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:44.330
While the mantra seems like a good one for
the film, the question is, why do these four

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:44.860
say it?

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:49.000
Both Chris Evans and Robert Downey Jr. have
been rumored to be approaching the end of

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:53.260
their time in the MCU, but the thought that
four of the original six Avengers are ready

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:57.460
to do "whatever it takes" could imply a larger
culling than anyone was expecting.

